    },
    {
      "claim": "HLM intrinsic clearance values for the scaffold class are moderate to high at 120 to 289.5 microliters per minute per milligram, a mechanistic presystemic-loss risk for the query high logD, but no direct low-F outcome transfers from these records.",
      "card_ids": ["C223", "C255", "C262"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C223", "C238", "C240", "C245", "C248", "C250", "C254", "C255", "C262"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct query-specific absolute oral bioavailability or IV versus oral AUC comparison is available.",
    "No direct F value is reported for the query or its closest analogs.",
    "No query-specific hepatic clearance measurement exists; HLM values are for related scaffold compounds.",
    "No query-specific fasted-state solubility or dissolution measurement is available; high logD is only a proxy.",
    "No formulation or clinical dose is specified for the query, so the impact of solubility and first-pass loss on F cannot be quantified."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L6 confirms hepatic CYP3A metabolism is the major clearance route for this scaffold class, a mechanistic presystemic-loss risk, but the same-scaffold drugs acalabrutinib and zanubrutinib are clinically used orally, so this does not establish F below 20 percent. Combined with L5 no-efflux evidence and L3 rapid absorption, F at or above 20 percent remains better supported. Prediction high with moderate confidence."
}

